# The kernel commit this app is built and tested against.
#
# One line, `<repo> <sha>`. `.github/workflows/ci.yml` reads it and checks that
# revision out; `frontend/src/kernel/README.md` has the local build command.
#
# Moving this pin is a commit in THIS repo, deliberately. It makes "the app
# adopted a new kernel" a reviewable change with a diff, instead of an ambient
# fact about whichever working tree happened to be next door. See the kernel's
# ADR-0003.
#
# A full SHA, not a branch: a branch would make CI's answer depend on when it
# ran. Same reason `tools/gen-fixtures.mjs` over there pins a revision rather
# than reading the working tree.
hunterMotko/shed-cad-rs 8dc68b0ad30b70fffd811b2eb56b9a719c28200a
